Generated-frame quality options, each behind its own [ofxr] key (0 by default: every composition byte for byte as before,
checked against the build without it on the NVIDIA occlusion and DCS motion fixtures' output hashes), read at the session's start and
followed live like the flow keys (0066: LiveFlow / Snapshot fg_quality, kLiveFgQuality, a rebuild on change). NVIDIA path
only; shader bits in UseGameMotion 16-23 of the pack and the compositions (D3D12FrameSynthesizer::quality_bits), bit 18
saying the frames are read linear (an sRGB view: the periphery or a composed swapchain; Quad Views' focus layer is UNORM
and holds encoded values).
  dcs_motion_sky_occlusion  MV path: a sky pixel whose two samples differ by more than 25 % of the brighter (linear
                            light) takes one frame's sample: an object's own vector whose fixed point holds here
                            (probed around), else the frame whose end the class atlas calls sky (night ghost of a grey
                            aircraft over a near-black sky: trailing copy 6-11 -> 0.02-0.08 MAE).
  perceptual_checks         every colour check (rgb_error) compares sRGB-encoded values on a linear-read image.
  flow_input_srgb           the flow engine's input sRGB-encoded on a linear-read image (night: about 40 levels below
                            0.02 instead of 17).
  low_confidence_current    the low-confidence fallback is the current frame at the pixel, not the two frames there
                            cross-faded.
  nvidia_edge_choice        where the four flow vectors spread over 1.5 px, the one of them or their mix whose ends
                            agree best (skips 0030's fixed point when a grid vector is taken).
  nvidia_temporal_hints     the engine's temporal hints for consecutive pairs (reset at a prime, retire, a pair that
                            does not follow, a field of view moved over 2 %, a rebuild).
  dcs_motion_mask_band      the MVs also inside the cockpit mask where the class atlas says world at the pixel and at
                            the vector's current end.
  foveated_fade_flow        focus layer, in its fade: the vector goes over to the periphery layer's (fill=2's link).
GPU (5424x5356 x2, 240 pairs, sRGB view): composition and pack unchanged within the bench's noise (+-10 us, +-3 us).

